{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Learn about the current capabilities of OpenUSD in Swift"}],"sections":[],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"OpenUSD in Swift is currently evolving and may change in the future. Here are some key features currently supported:"}]},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Reference-types-in-Swift","level":3,"text":"Reference types in Swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"UsdStage and SdfLayer are imported as classes in Swift and behave like classes written in Swift. When Swift passes a raw pointer to UsdStage or SdfLayer, Swift automatically increments or decrements the underlying reference count as needed, allowing Swift or C++ to influence the lifetime of the same UsdStage or SdfLayer."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["func makeTempStage() -> pxr.UsdStage {","    return Overlay.Dereference(pxr.UsdStage.CreateNew(\"\/tmp\/myStage.usda\", .LoadAll))","}","","func defineXform(_ stage: pxr.UsdStage, _ path: pxr.SdfPath) {","    stage.DefinePrim(path, .UsdGeomTokens.Xform)","}","","let stage = makeTempStage()","defineXform(stage, \"\/hello\")","let layer = Overlay.Dereference(stage.GetRootLayer())","layer.Save(false)"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"See ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/WhatIsAForeignReferenceType"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SwiftUsd\/documentation\/SwiftUsd\/ForeignReferenceTypesAndSmartPointers"},{"text":" for more information.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","style":"warning","content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"When working in Swift, do not use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TfRefPtr.pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"TfWeakPtr.pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" to dereference Pixar’s smart pointers, as the "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"pointee"},{"type":"text","text":" property is unsafe. Use "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Overlay.Dereference(_:TfRefPtr)"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Overlay.Dereference(_:TfWeakPtr)"},{"type":"text","text":" instead."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"name":"Warning"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"Swift-protocol-conformances","level":3,"text":"Swift protocol conformances"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Many OpenUSD types conform to one or more of the following protocols:","type":"text"}]},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Equatable"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Hashable"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Identifiable"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"CustomStringConvertible","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ExpressibleByStringLiteral","type":"codeVoice"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ExpressibleByArrayLiteral","type":"codeVoice"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sequence"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Sendable"}]}]}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["let token: pxr.TfToken = \"my custom token\" \/\/ TfToken conforms to ExpressibleByStringLiteral","var prims: Set<pxr.UsdPrim> = Set<pxr.UsdPrim>() \/\/ UsdPrim conforms to Hashable","let numbers: pxr.VtIntArray = [1, 2, 3] \/\/ VtIntArray conforms to ExpressibleByArrayLiteral"],"syntax":"swift"},{"type":"heading","anchor":"TfNotice-support","level":3,"text":"TfNotice support"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Swift code can register for ","ty